<urn:atm:triage:finding/AW-READY-N1>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AW-READY-N1" ;
  triage:title "tracing_bridge tests busy-poll the retained JSONL file with a 2s wall-clock cap and no synchronization with the async flush worker, silently returning partial content on expiry" ;
  triage:description "fenix reviewer-B flaky/racy test audit (01M1S72R6GNBE5ZETPK6943JMX). crates/atm-observability/src/tracing_bridge.rs:451-462 lines() helper (used by ac1 :464, ac2 :487, ac5 :547) busy-polls atm.log.jsonl for >= N lines with a 2s wall-clock cap; nothing synchronizes with the async flush worker; on expiry it silently returns partial content instead of failing loudly, masking real flush failures as false negatives/positives under load. Redesign: test-only RetainedLogger::flush() delegating to sc_observability::Logger::flush() (runtime.rs:176, synchronous), then one deterministic read; delete the deadline loop. Same class of defect as pre-existing Family C (test flakiness), found by a dedicated audit rather than a CI failure trigger." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-aw" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "test-determinism" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
